      {
        "id": 229713,
        "name": "catDreaming",
        "username": "catDreaming",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/4491bb/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-02-07T16:33:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I generally allow my players to make Overcome actions to untick boxes from the scene tracker, but there is emphasis that doing so makes you look more dangerous to the villains and environment. Oh, you spent your turn without anything to really do unticking a box on the scene tracker? Turns out that a&nbsp;second Blade Battalion just came around the corner, and they're now converging on you.</p>\n<p>In general, I find that Twists tend to be both an incentive to players to make Overcomes, and a deterent against making them needlessly.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:04:32.239Z",
